    <summary>Writes selected mailboxes from a Microsoft Exchange .edb database into Outlook PST files on the local PC, keeping folder trees, attachments and dates, with this edb to pst converter.</summary>
    <description>This package installs an edb to pst converter for Windows PCs that extracts mail from a Microsoft Exchange mailbox database file and saves it for Outlook. It fits a contractor or admin who deploys tools with Chocolatey to a recovery PC, receives a copy of the .edb after a server failure and must recover mailbox data for each user without bringing Exchange online again.

![EDB to PST Converter Tool screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/edb/edb-v1-main.png)

## How to use EDB to PST Converter Software

1. Load the .edb file. The program scans it offline, and a tree of mailboxes and their folders appears in the interface.
2. Check the mailboxes and folders you want. Select a folder to list its messages and select a message to preview it before export.
3. Open the Convert page to enter a date range, leave out Deleted Items or Junk, and decide on images.
4. Choose an output location for the PST and click Start. Progress is shown while it runs, and Stop cancels the job.

Trial note: until it is registered, the program works as a free trial and exports a limited sample of messages. A license lifts the sample limit.

![EDB to PST Converter Tool screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/edb/edb-v1-filter.png)

## Convert EDB to PST by mailbox, folder and date

Each mailbox in the database gets its own checkbox, and so does each folder under it. That lets you recover mail for one person, a single project folder or many accounts in one pass. With From and To dates set through the drop-down calendar, only items from that window are written, which keeps a PST for an audit or a litigation request small. Leaving out the trash and spam folders trims it further.

## What an Exchange EDB to PST export keeps

- The folder structure of each mailbox, maintained as on the server.
- Subject, HTML body, sender and recipients including Cc, and message dates.
- Email attachments in their exact original form, and inline pictures inside HTML mail.
- Read and unread flags.

The software converts mail to the Unicode PST file format that Outlook opens. The database is parsed by its own x64 helper, and databases over 2 GB show a warning before the run.

![EDB to PST Converter Tool screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/edb/edb-v1-run.png)

## Who it is for

- Exchange admins left with a dismounted database after a crash, or who migrate users and want mail kept private.
- IT contractors and forensic examiners who receive an .edb copy and must export EDB mail as mailbox PST files.
- Teams that install the edb to pst converter tool on several PCs through Chocolatey and work where neither Exchange nor Outlook is present.

One database opens at a time, so multiple EDB files are processed in turn. Exchange 2010 and older, public folders, live servers, Microsoft 365, repair of corrupt files, PST split and MSG output are out of scope.

## Trial and license

The package installs the free trial of a commercial program, and full use requires a license. A lifetime, 1-year or business license removes the sample limit, and the [EDB file to PST export](https://www.softorbits.net/edb-to-pst-converter/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) page lists the options.

## FAQ

### How do I convert EDB to PST?

Open the .edb file, tick the mailboxes and folders, set any filters and click Start.

### Is there an Exchange EDB to PST converter for Windows?

Yes. This program reads Exchange 2013, 2016 and 2019 databases on a local Windows PC and writes PST files from them.

### What does a PST converter do?

It takes mail stored in another format and writes it into a PST, the data file Outlook opens. Here the source is an Exchange mailbox database, and folders, attachments and dates carry over.
